{
  "id": "QA-UNIT-REG-PR-948-site-publish-flow-happy",
  "itemIds": ["regression:REG-PR-948-site-publish-flow"],
  "requirement": "Publishing a site at its Tracy address: one operation at a time, the flag only after the host's job is done and said so, no way round go-live, an unconfirmed operation held until its real outcome, and no button a role would be refused — and, since part 2, the site's own domain through the same operation: DNS shown only as measured, cleanups recorded half done and continued under the same key, and operations nobody reads settled in the background — and, since the review after #988, no bare domain reserved for ever, no name held without proof past 72 hours, and the site-connect-domain switch closing the doors that start an own domain",
  "oracle": {
    "source": "tests/regression/cases/REG-PR-948-site-publish-flow.json",
    "ref": "PR #948 (feat); fix evidence: Before the change (base e5aecf517, origin/develop with nothing of this change): the new and changed test files run against the base sources exit 1 — 85 of 102 fail, 61 of them behaviour assertions (the door answered 200/published at once, no PUBLISH_BUSY, the state door set the flag, a body with domains reached the host, a host body of `null` answered 500, a failed required step of go-live.sh still ended 0, the Settings address was worked out before the CMS read, no chip, no Publish button). Review after #988 (base c999b8370): the eleven new tests of site-address.test.mjs run against the base sources on a PostgreSQL of the run: 8 fail by their own assertions — `example.com at PUT /address: 202 !== 400`; an aged reservation still held (`409 !== 202` for the second site); the switch off still answered `409 !== 403`; the sweep let nothing go — and the guard that a proven name is never taken passes on both trees.",
    "invariant": "EXIT1 === 0, FAIL1 === 0, SKIP1 === 0. EXIT2 === 0, FAIL2 === 0, SKIP2 === 0. GUARD, FLAG, ROLES, STRANGERS, STATEDOOR, NODOMAINS, UNCONFIRMED, REASKED, CLOSINGLINE, NOOUTCOME, HELD, BUSY, SWEEP, SAMEMS, ONESNAPSHOT, OLDPOLL, STATEKEYS, ONREAD, LISTOP, FRESHREAD, QUEUEDLOST, RUNNINGLOST, UNVERIFIED, ACCEPTED, NOGRACE, LOSTACK, TAKENHELD, NEVERTAKEN, RECORDLOST, MARKUNREAD and MARKWRITE are each 'ok' (before this change: the door answered 200 with publish 'published' as soon as the host took the job, two presses started two jobs, the state door set the flag by itself, and any domain in the body reached the host). HOSTGUARD, HOSTBODY, JOBKEY, RERUN, SCRIPTSTEPS, SCRIPTAPACHE, FIREWALLREAD, GOLIVELOCK, SNAPSHOTORDER, EDITOR, RELOAD, DOUBLE, UNREAD, WAITING, SITESWITCH, OTHERSITE, DIALOG, OTHERTAB, UNOBSERVED, STORELOST, FIREWALLCHECK, ROWPUBLISHING, LISTORDER, NAMELESS, REFUSALLIST, KEYFIRST, TAKENSAID, KEYTURN, STOREUNREAD, MARKED, MARKFIRST, MARKFAIL, MARKUNKNOWN and NOMARK are each 'ok'. DNSREAD, LATELOOKUP, BADNAMES, TOKENOWNER, CARRIED, NOTPROVEN, HALFDONE, REMOVEOP, ONEOP, DELETEHELD, SWEEPSTART, SWEEPAGE, SWEEPBACKOFF, SWEEPREPLICAS, NOAUTORETRY, FOLLOWUPKEPT are each 'ok' (before part 2: no domain reached the host, a domain read ready from one stored flag with no word on what was looked up, nothing swept an operation nobody read, and a go-live follow-up was dropped after a day). NOTUNNEL, TUNNELONLY, SIGNAL, SIGNALREAL, RUNSIGNAL, ATTEMPT, DROPJOB, TARGETDOOR, LEDGER, DRAFTPARTIAL, DROPSCRIPT, INGRESSBACK, INGRESSANSWERS, ONLYPORT, EVENTOP, EVENTFAIL, DOMSTATES, DOMRECORDS, NOINFER, DOMROLES are each 'ok' (before part 2: every go-live answered 501 on a host with no tunnel configuration, a script killed by a signal was recorded as exit code 1, a failed cleanup could only be answered with the failure it had, and the publish event fired only when the flag moved). BOTHHALVES, LEDGERWRITE, LOCKKINDS, ADDOWNED, SHORTANSWER, INGRESSLOCK, TEARDOWNKEYED, ROWDELETING, DELETETAKES, DELETEFAILED, DELETESWEPT, DELETEMARK, DELETEPENDING, DELETESAID, DNSORDER, BODYSHAPE are each 'ok' (before the review round: a removal was said before the record was rewritten; an add replaced a rule that led to another port; a short provider answer read as an empty list; the delete door looked for an operation and then erased the row whatever the teardown did; two lookups could land in either order; unknown body fields were dropped). APEX, APEXLEGACY, LAPSE, RENEW, PROVENKEPT, LATELAPSE, PROOFORDER, PROOFLOCK, PROOFLOCKONLY, TAKEOVERLOCK, SWEEPWAIT, LEGACYNAMES, LAPSESWEEP, LAPSERACE, SWITCHOFF, SWITCHUNREAD, STRICTSWITCH, DOMAPEX, DOMAPEXLEGACY, DOMAPEXFAILED, DOMUNCONNECTABLE, DOMLAPSED, DOMLAPSEDREMOVE, PARSELAPSED and PARSEAPEX are each 'ok' (before the review fix, on c999b8370: `PUT …/address {name: 'example.com', kind: 'custom'}` answered 202; a reservation aged 73 hours still answered another site NAME_TAKEN, and neither the sweep nor a reserve let it go; with `site-connect-domain` off, reserving answered 409/202 instead of 403 OWN_DOMAIN_DISABLED).",
